{"nodes": [{"id": "changelog_v0_2_0", "label": "Release 0.2.0 (2026-08-06)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "## 0.2.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_v0_1_0", "label": "Release 0.1.0", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "## 0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_ollama_context_window_fix", "label": "Fix: Ollama context window assumed 4096", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Fixed", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not cosmetic: auto-compaction fires against the window, so a 262144-token cloud model was being summarised away every couple of rounds. smith now asks Ollama's own /api/show."}, {"id": "changelog_context_gauge_overfull_fix", "label": "Fix: context gauge hid an over-full window", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Fixed", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Printing max(window, used) made 181% of a wrongly-detected window read as a normal full window."}, {"id": "changelog_provider_id_label_fix", "label": "Fix: every Ollama session recorded as OpenAI", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Fixed", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "OpenAiProvider::id() was hardcoded; it prices turns and labels turns.provider. Stored costs were always right, only the label was wrong, so no migration is needed."}, {"id": "changelog_home_as_project_root_fix", "label": "Fix: home directory could become the project root", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Fixed", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "~/.smith is a root marker and always exists, so any project without .git resolved to $HOME \u2014 loading ~/SMITH.md twice and widening the @import jail to the whole home directory."}, {"id": "changelog_text_file_busy_fix", "label": "Fix: 'Text file busy' verifying a downloaded browser", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Fixed", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Between fork and exec a subprocess started by another thread holds an inherited write descriptor to the binary and execve refuses; the probe now retries."}, {"id": "changelog_sidebar_tabs", "label": "Sidebar tabs (Session / Tasks / Vitals)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Added \u2014 Terminal UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stacked in one column the four sections did not fit a 24-row terminal."}, {"id": "changelog_diagnostics_panel", "label": "Ctrl+L diagnostics panel and tracing subscriber", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Added \u2014 Terminal UI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Until now no tracing subscriber was installed anywhere in the workspace, so every warning the MCP client and provider adapters emitted was discarded."}, {"id": "changelog_session_cost_from_turn_ledger", "label": "Session cost reported from per-turn figures", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "### Changed", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A resumed session used to display today's prices applied to the whole session's tokens, disagreeing with what it had actually spent."}, {"id": "changelog_language_pinning", "label": "Answers pinned to the user's language", "file_type": "concept", "source